"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"I’d choose the earlier-arriving of the two selected award journeys shown, provided you can accept a separate-ticket connection in Los Angeles. The tradeoff: its award taxes and seat availability are unconfirmed, and the positioning flight is not on the same ticket.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J75@2027-01-08T08:40-08:00/SFO>BKK/B>2027-01-10T04:15\",\"n\":\"Recommended: earlier Bangkok arrival\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO January 8 at 8:40 a.m. and arrives in Bangkok January 10 at 4:15 a.m. local time. The journey combines an Alaska SFO–LAX flight, quoted at USD 59 with unknown quote scope, and a Turkish Airlines award from LAX via Istanbul to Bangkok. The award is reported as business class and costs 275,000 Turkish program points; its award taxes are unknown. Its Istanbul connection is 2 hours 20 minutes. The main gain over the other selected award journey is earlier arrival; the downside is the same separate-ticket risk and unknown award taxes and seats.\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T02\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T03\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J115@2027-01-08T08:40-08:00/SFO>BKK/B>2027-01-10T08:50\",\"n\":\"Alternative: longer Istanbul connection\",\"v\":\"This also departs SFO January 8 at 8:40 a.m. and uses an Alaska SFO–LAX flight quoted at USD 59, then a Turkish Airlines award from LAX via Istanbul to Bangkok. The award is reported as business class and costs 275,000 Turkish program points; award taxes are unknown. It arrives January 10 at 8:50 a.m. local time, with a 7-hour Istanbul connection. Choose it only if that later arrival and longer connection suit you better; it does not offer an earlier arrival than the recommendation.\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T01\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C1@2027-01-08T06:05-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"Cash baseline: SFO to Bangkok\",\"v\":\"A separate SFO–Bangkok cash itinerary is quoted at USD 452, with unknown quote scope. It departs January 8 at 6:05 a.m. and arrives January 10 at 12:20 a.m. Bangkok local time, with two stops via Seattle and Seoul on Delta and Korean Air. This is a cash-fare reference, not a like-for-like total-cost comparison with either award: the award taxes and the scopes of the cash quotes are unknown.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"Shared cautions: both award options report one stop on the LAX–Istanbul–Bangkok award and a 149-minute wait at LAX between the Alaska positioning flight and the award. The tickets are separate, and protection or bookability across that join is unverified. Both awards report business class, but the cabin for each flight leg is absent; seat availability is unknown, and the program does not reliably provide award taxes. The USD 59 positioning-fare quote has unknown scope, so it is not an all-in price. Confirm current availability and prices with the booking providers; the search results are not real-time. The shown choices are selected examples, not the full inventory, and the search reports partial provider coverage.\"}]}"
